Voice acceptance behavior
When the caller interrupts:
- Cancel obsolete LLM generation.
- Cancel obsolete TTS generation.
- Clear queued playback.
- Reject late results from the old response.
- Respond to the newest caller turn.
Do not assume that installing Silero or setting one SDK option proves all of this works.
Latency contract
Keep the existing acceptance target:
p95 below 500 ms from the caller’s actual end of speech to the first meaningful audible agent response at the caller endpoint.
Include endpointing, processing, transport, and playback.
Internal timing logs are not equivalent to caller-perceived latency. Mark the target unmeasured until it is actually measured.
